<resources>
    <!-- Pre-Compose window background, matching the Pelagic (dark) surface. -->
    <color name="gridlink_window_background">#0E1A1F</color>
    <!-- Splash field, dark: GridlinkNightColors.background, for the same reason the light one is
         GridlinkDayColors.background — the splash hands straight over to GridlinkIntroOverlay,
         which paints that exact fill. See values/colors.xml for the full note, including why this
         resource can only ever be approximately right.

         ⚠️ Night's and not OLED's (#000000), and the choice does not matter: the two are four
         points apart on one channel and the step between them is not visible on any panel. Day is
         the case that had to be got right, being a saturated blue behind what used to be a
         near-white field. -->
    <color name="gridlink_splash_background">#050A14</color>
</resources>
